        <type>void</type>
        <definition>static void DbProbe::check</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>check</name>
        <qualifiedname>DbProbe::check</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Guards a database-access point against running on an IO thread. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername><ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref></parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If called while a <ref refid="classDbProbe" kindref="compound">DbProbe</ref> is active on this thread.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> helpers call this first; in probe mode it throws before any connection is leased, allowing the request to be re-run from the start on a DB worker where no probe is active. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="src/database/dbprobe.hpp" line="86" column="17" bodyfile="src/database/dbprobe.hpp" bodystart="86" bodyend="92"/>
        <references refid="classDbProbe_1a86209915d051bd2999972e9e448d00c2" compoundref="dbprobe_8hpp" startline="95">active_</references>
        <referencedby refid="classDatabaseController_1a17754cf11f19b559b1fd8c3077817556" compoundref="databasecontroller_8hpp" startline="283" endline="329">DatabaseController::executer</referencedby>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>RAII marker that puts the current thread in &quot;probe&quot; mode. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>While an instance is alive, <ref refid="classDbProbe_1af3b9ebe61addb4dd1885a3d117221a1f" kindref="member">DbProbe::check()</ref> throws <ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref> on that thread, preventing any database access from running on a Drogon IO thread. The active flag is <computeroutput>thread_local</computeroutput>, so only the constructing thread is affected. Instances are stack-allocated within a try block in the request wrapper and must not be shared across threads. Non-copyable and non-assignable. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The destructor unconditionally clears the flag; nested probes on the same thread would clear it early, so usage assumes a single probe per thread at a time. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="structWouldBlock" kindref="compound">WouldBlock</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
